% A rule base with a facts background (language reference §14.5).
%
% The rules read "the kind of a garment" and "the fabric construction of a
% garment". A shop listing does not speak in these words. It says "Tee
% Shirt" and "Craft of Weaving: Knit". The two background programs say what
% such words mean, and what is taken to be so when a listing is silent.
%
% The system never reasons with the background. Only "Write it in English"
% (and the editor's assistant) use it, when they read facts from a text:
%   1. Open this program, and open the Scenario Editor.
%   2. Click "Write it in English", and paste: "Men Tee Shirt. Craft of
%      Weaving: Knit."
%   3. The reader notes what the listing says. The background rules then add
%      "the kind of the shirt is T-shirt" and the other facts that follow.
%      Each fact says which background program gave it, and by which rule.
%
% The scenario "read" shows the result. The query "readings" gives the two
% readings: the strict reading admits the listing and the garment words
% only; the full reading also admits the presumptions.

the target language is: prolog.

the facts background includes these resources:
    background/garment_words, background/garment_presumptions.

the functions are:
    the fabric construction of *a garment* is *a construction*; undefined.

the templates are:
    the kind of *a garment* is *a kind*; undefined.
    the fabric of *a garment* is lightweight; undefined.
    the heading of *a garment* is *a heading*.
    *a garment* is classified in *a heading* by *a reading*.

the knowledge base shirts includes:

the heading of a garment is 6109
    if the kind of the garment is T-shirt
    and the fabric construction of the garment is knitted
    and the fabric of the garment is lightweight.

the heading of a garment is 6205
    if the kind of the garment is shirt
    and the fabric construction of the garment is woven.

a garment is classified in a heading by a reading
    if the reading is in [strict reading, full reading]
    and the heading of the garment is the heading
        according to the reading.

the listing is admissible under strict reading.
the listing is admissible under full reading.
garment words is admissible under strict reading.
garment words is admissible under full reading.
garment presumptions is admissible under full reading.

scenario stated is, as stated in the listing:
    the kind of tee is T-shirt.
    the fabric construction of tee is knitted.
    the fabric of tee is lightweight.
    headings expects answers ["the heading of tee is 6109"].

scenario read is, as stated in the listing:
    the fabric construction of tee is knitted, according to garment words, because "construction_by_field", confer "Craft of Weaving: Knit".
    the kind of tee is T-shirt, according to garment words, because "kind_by_name", confer "Men Tee Shirt".
    the fabric of tee is lightweight, according to garment presumptions, because "tshirt_fabric", confer "Men Tee Shirt".
    readings expects answers ["tee is classified in 6109 by full reading"].

query headings is:
    the heading of which garment is which heading.

query readings is:
    which garment is classified in which heading by which reading.
